from scripts.curate_remaining import Batch
b=Batch('06-clinical-tools',['Biomedical Engineering','Clinical Medicine','Pharmacology','Anesthesiology','Emergency Medicine','Surgery','Orthopedics','Ophthalmology','Dermatology']);a=b.a;u=b.u
# Candidate delivery, sensing and control methods are not clinical efficacy claims.
a('MEC-08','BME-09','Qualified soft-contact mechanics could supply a joint/interface component of a body-mechanics model.','A contact law does not predict every organ’s disease progression or treatment outcome.','enabling')
a('LON-08','CLM-02','A qualified proteostasis intervention could be tested where a defined protein-handling defect is causally relevant.','No shared root cause across neurodegenerative disease or complete cognitive restoration is assumed.','enabling')
a('PHA-04','ONC-02','An identified transporter target could motivate tests in a defined efflux-mediated resistance setting.','A target is not a safe inhibitor, and pump inhibition would not eradicate every metastatic tumor.')
a('PHA-08','EMR-06','A qualified neutralizing molecule could be one component of an antidote platform for specified exposures.','A class-specific reaction does not cover every poison, metabolite, overdose or clinical kinetic requirement.','enabling')
a('PHA-09','DER-01','A pharmacological regeneration trigger could be screened in a full-thickness skin repair model.','Triggering growth does not establish appendages, innervation, scarlessness or safe clinical repair.','enabling')
a('PHA-09','ORT-08','A candidate regeneration trigger could be tested for a defined fracture-repair mechanism.','It does not establish rapid union, a single-dose protocol or efficacy in compromised bone.','enabling')
a('PHA-10','ANS-08','Self-regulating release could be investigated as one drug-delivery actuator in a defined anesthesia controller.','Molecular concentration control does not establish anesthetic depth, hemodynamic stability or zero risk.','enabling')
a('PHA-10','OPH-08','A qualified feedback-release mechanism could be one formulation route to test for a selected posterior-segment agent.','Duration, payload stability, local toxicity and no burst release over years are not established.','enabling')
a('NEU-08','ANS-01','A causal account of anesthetic state transitions could motivate candidate reversal targets.','Awareness is not every anesthetic effect; respiratory, analgesic and other drug actions may require separate control.','enabling')
a('NEU-08','ANS-04','Defined state mechanisms could help propose measurable indicators for monitoring studies.','A mechanism does not provide a 100%-accurate real-time consciousness measurement.')
a('ANS-04','ANS-08','A qualified depth estimate could be a feedback input to a delivery controller.','Monitoring accuracy is unestablished, and measurement alone does not prevent every dosing or physiologic failure.','enabling')
a('ANS-01','ANS-08','A qualified reversal intervention could provide one recovery action for a constrained controller.','Reversal does not guarantee safe autonomous operation or recovery from every complication.')
a('BME-07','ANS-05','A qualified editing platform could deliver a candidate correction for a specified susceptibility variant.','Delivery does not establish every malignant-hyperthermia mechanism, correction efficacy or absence of adverse effects.','enabling')
a('NEU-04','ANS-07','Candidate neural-repair regulators could be screened in a defined peripheral-nerve injury model.','Brain/adult regeneration concepts do not automatically transfer to peripheral conduction or sensory-motor recovery.')
a('ANS-09','CLM-05','A qualified post-surgical transition mechanism could identify subtype-specific targets for a pain-modulation program.','A particular pain mechanism does not establish all chronic-pain control, preservation of acute pain or no addiction.')
a('ANS-08','ANS-10','A qualified delivery controller could be evaluated as one component of a tailored high-risk anesthesia protocol.','Autonomy does not remove cardiopulmonary risk or establish safety in every severely ill patient.')
a('MIC-10','EMR-02','A host-response model could help choose a restricted microbial-metabolite/receptor hypothesis to test in an infection model.','No metabolite is assumed to cause all septic shock; a map is not a single-dose reversal therapy.')
a('BME-04','EMR-03','A qualified portable scanner could provide one acquisition channel for a defined emergency diagnostic system.','Image acquisition does not establish disease-specific interpretation or 100% diagnosis of every emergency.','enabling')
a('BCH-06','EMR-05','An energy-coupling model could help formulate bounded metabolic-suppression experiments.','Disrupting energy production can be harmful; no protective suspended-animation protocol follows from mechanism knowledge.')
a('NEU-03','EMR-08','A memory-consolidation model could motivate selective intervention hypotheses to test after a defined traumatic exposure.','A memory mechanism does not establish PTSD causation, safe selectivity or universal prevention.','enabling')
a('BME-01','EMR-10','A qualified regeneration pathway could be investigated in an acute-injury model as a candidate repair component.','No immediate timescale, restored organ function or golden-hour clinical benefit is established.','enabling')
a('OPT-05','SUR-02','For an optical route with wavefront distortion, correction could be investigated as an imaging subsystem.','Correction does not establish penetration, molecular specificity, cellular resolution in every tissue or a surgical instrument.','enabling')
a('SUR-02','SUR-03','A qualified live tissue image could supply anatomy/state observations for a surgical control policy.','Images do not provide judgment, safe actions or error-free surgery.','enabling')
a('ROB-01','SUR-03','A qualified manipulation system could provide a tool-handling component of a surgical robot.','Surgical forces, anatomy, sterility and judgment require separate validation.','enabling')
a('ROB-09','SUR-03','Specified controller proofs could help constrain candidate surgical decisions.','Model-based proofs do not cover every unexpected anatomy, bleeding event or hardware failure.')
a('IMM-09','SUR-04','A qualified antigen-specific tolerance method could be investigated in a specified donor/recipient setting.','It does not establish permanent donor tolerance without infection, malignancy or other adverse effects.','enabling')
a('BME-04','SUR-06','A qualified molecular/localization image could help define a candidate deep-lesion target.','Localization does not supply precise energy delivery, repair or protection of adjacent tissue.','enabling')
a('BME-06','SUR-07','Directed assembly could provide a candidate scaffold architecture across a specified nerve gap.','A scaffold does not establish axon guidance, circuit reconnection or normal conduction.','enabling')
a('BME-07','SUR-09','A qualified delivery/reprogramming platform could be adapted for a specified intraoperative application.','Local timing, target specificity, functional correction and safety need independent evaluation.','enabling')
a('BME-06','SUR-10','Directed tissue assembly could provide a fabrication route to test for a proposed operative construct.','It does not establish same-session readiness, autologous tissue viability or a functioning organ.','enabling')
a('BME-06','ORT-01','A cell/tissue-assembly implementation could be tested as one route for a cartilage-repair construct.','It is not a demonstrated inducible repair pathway or proof of native thickness, mechanics and durability.','enabling')
a('BME-09','ORT-03','A qualified tissue-mechanics model could compare candidate tendon/enthesis restoration designs.','Predicted mechanics do not induce healing or establish zero scar and native integration.')
a('CRM-09','ORT-04','A suitable scaffold-forming bioceramic could be one material component in an assembly-based bone-repair design.','Printability, intraoperative use, vascularization and safe loading are not supplied by a bioceramic ambition.','enabling')
a('LON-03','ORT-07','A qualified selective-clearance method could be tested for the senescent-cell component explicitly named by this joint-treatment ambition.','Clearance does not establish cartilage homeostasis, subchondral repair or reversal at every stage.','enabling')
a('MEC-08','ORT-09','Soft-contact predictions could help compare a proposed meniscus/labrum construct under a specified joint load.','They do not provide tissue fabrication, vascularization, integration or lifetime function.')
a('BIO-07','ORT-10','A qualified growth-control mechanism could motivate tests of localized skeletal shaping.','Growing and adult bone have different constraints; safe real-time reshaping without mechanical intervention is not established.','enabling')
a('NEU-04','OPH-01','Candidate neural-repair regulators could be tested in a defined retinal/optic-nerve model.','They do not establish replacement of every retinal cell type or complete synaptic reconnection.','enabling')
a('OPH-01','OPH-02','A qualified retinal repair method could address one cell-restoration component of a glaucoma intervention.','Neural repair does not restore aqueous outflow or establish a permanent one-time cure.','enabling')
a('BME-07','OPH-04','Non-viral targeted delivery could be one research route for a specified retinal editing program.','Every mutation, payload, cell target and lifelong outcome requires separate evaluation.','alternative-route',group='retinal-delivery')
a('VIR-07','OPH-04','A qualified viral vector could be another delivery approach for a specified retinal program.','Precise vector design and immune safety are not established; routes may combine.','alternative-route',group='retinal-delivery')
a('BIO-07','OPH-05','A tissue-sizing model could motivate candidate pathways to test in a defined axial-growth model.','It does not identify a safe drug or establish complete prevention of childhood myopia.')
a('BME-06','OPH-06','A qualified assembly method could provide a fabrication route for a patient-specific corneal construct.','Transparency, innervation, immune compatibility and lifelong integration remain independent.','enabling')
a('SUR-02','OPH-07','A qualified live molecular image could provide a targeting channel for a selected ocular intervention.','It does not supply non-thermal ablation, tumor specificity or preserved vision.','enabling')
a('BME-02','OPH-10','A qualified neural interface could provide a stimulation/communication channel in a visual-prosthesis design.','A channel does not establish image encoding, safe perception or the stated visual acuity.','enabling')
a('IMM-09','DER-02','If a defined skin-disease subgroup has an appropriate antigen-driven mechanism, a tolerance method could test selective immune reset.','No causal antigen or permanent barrier-restoring treatment is identified here; the assumption may fail.')
a('LON-03','DER-03','Selective clearance could be investigated for the senescent-cell component explicitly named in the skin-aging ambition.','It would not establish collagen restoration, DNA repair or complete reversal of photoaging.','enabling')
a('BME-06','DER-05','A tissue-assembly process could provide a fabrication route for selected autologous skin constructs.','Appendages, vascularization, innervation and lifelong integration need independent evidence.','enabling')
a('SUR-02','DER-06','A qualified cellular/molecular image could provide a margin-observation channel in a skin-tumor procedure.','It does not establish non-invasive classification, all cancer-cell visibility or complete excision.','enabling')
a('LON-07','DER-07','A qualified stem-function regulator could be screened in a defined melanocyte restoration setting.','Stem-cell activation does not establish durable pigmentation or removal of the process causing recurrence.','enabling')
a('BME-07','DER-08','Non-viral delivery could be one research route for a specified skin-cell editing intervention.','No all-mutation coverage, lifelong effect or zero off-target risk is established.','alternative-route',group='skin-delivery')
a('VIR-07','DER-08','A qualified vector could be another delivery route for a specified skin-cell intervention.','Tissue access, payloads and immune responses still require evaluation.','alternative-route',group='skin-delivery')
a('PHA-09','DER-09','A candidate regenerative trigger could be tested in a defined chronic-wound repair model.','A growth signal does not correct every perfusion, infection or comorbidity constraint.','enabling')
for id,reason in {
'BME-10':'No defined carrier, coagulation-control or immune mechanism supplies the complete indefinite blood-function substitute; it is not treated as an automatic hemorrhage-control device.',
'CLM-01':'The systemic-aging master-pathway ambition overlaps LON-01. A complete aging-reversal goal is not a separate causal input to another complete aging-reversal goal.',
'CLM-04':'The original source explicitly flags equivalence to BME-01. Retain the duplicate metadata, not a goal-to-goal causal arrow.',
'CLM-06':'The liquid-biopsy ambition overlaps ONC-06; an imaging scanner does not establish a blood-based detection test or its specificity.',
'CLM-10':'The programmable antigen-tolerance platform overlaps IMM-09’s safe antigen-specific tolerance ambition; no separate intervening mechanism is specified.',
'PHA-02':'No specific orally delivered candidate and its target behavior are supplied. Better oral transport alone does not establish a listed root-cause cure.',
'PHA-06':'Resetting opioid tolerance does not create a non-opioid analgesic or remove every addiction pathway. A qualified disease-specific use still needs review.',
'ANS-02':'The non-addictive analgesic ambition overlaps CLM-05/EMR-09 at the outcome level but supplies no distinct molecular target to make a causal sequence.',
'ANS-03':'No qualified causal intervention for postoperative cognitive dysfunction is specified. A general sleep, memory or consciousness model is not prevention evidence.',
'ANS-06':'The difficult-airway device overlaps EMR-07’s airway goal. No reviewed airway geometry, ventilation or rescue mechanism establishes universal success.',
'EMR-01':'No defined resuscitation mechanism in the collection simultaneously restores circulation and all neurological function for every arrest cause.',
'EMR-04':'No qualified local/systemic hemostatic-control mechanism establishes stopping all bleeding without remote thrombosis; generic blood replacement does not suffice.',
'EMR-07':'This airway ambition overlaps ANS-06 while imposing non-invasive success. Neither complete airway outcome supplies a device mechanism for the other.',
'EMR-09':'No specific rapid non-opioid target and pharmacokinetic route are supplied; another complete analgesia aspiration is not a causal input.',
'SUR-01':'The original source flags equivalence to BME-01; keep its identity and duplicate reference without a causal alias arrow.',
'SUR-05':'The original source flags equivalence to BME-06; keep the surgical entry independently accessible, not as a downstream duplicate node.',
'SUR-08':'The source excludes clips, sutures and topical agents but supplies no alternative control mechanism. The emergency topical/systemic-agent ambition does not satisfy that restriction.',
'ORT-02':'No qualified bone-remodeling intervention is specified for rebuilding systemic architecture. General regeneration or cell growth is not a complete osteoporosis mechanism.',
'ORT-05':'The original source flags equivalence to NRL-02. Keep the spinal-regeneration reference as equivalence, not a prerequisite.',
'ORT-06':'The collection does not specify a qualified permanent implant-surface design combining anti-biofilm behavior and lifelong bone integration. A resorbing scaffold is not that surface.',
'OPH-03':'The no-adaptive-optics restriction excludes using the perfect adaptive-optics goal as its solution; no distinct retinal acquisition mechanism was identified.',
'OPH-09':'No reviewed pathway simultaneously supplies gland secretion, goblet cells and stable tear-film behavior; generic growth control does not establish a dry-eye cure.',
'DER-04':'No specific prevention mechanism or antigen design is supplied for all UV-induced and other skin cancers; a broad cancer-vaccine aspiration is not an efficacy argument.',
'DER-10':'Cell-size control does not specify the hair-follicle phase switch or safe lasting activation/suppression, so no growth-to-cycling causal arrow is justified.'
}.items():u(id,reason,'source-equivalence' if id in ['CLM-04','SUR-01','SUR-05','ORT-05'] else 'overlapping-target' if id in ['CLM-01','CLM-06','CLM-10','ANS-02','ANS-06','EMR-07','EMR-09'] else 'unresolved-mechanism')
b.reject('OPT-05','OPH-03','The retinal target explicitly excludes adaptive optics.')
b.reject('BME-04','CLM-06','An imaging device is not the source’s blood-test mechanism.')
b.reject('NEU-08','EMR-05','Loss of awareness is not protective metabolic suppression.')
b.reject('PHA-06','ANS-02','An opioid-tolerance reset does not supply a non-opioid drug.')
b.branch('anesthesia-control','Anesthesia sensing and control',['NEU-08','ANS-01','ANS-04','PHA-10','ANS-08','ANS-10'])
b.branch('surgical-components','Surgical sensing, control and delivery',['OPT-05','SUR-02','ROB-01','ROB-09','SUR-03','BME-07','SUR-09','IMM-09','SUR-04'])
b.branch('retinal-routes','Retinal repair, delivery and interfaces',['NEU-04','OPH-01','OPH-02','BME-07','VIR-07','OPH-04','BME-02','OPH-10'])
b.branch('skin-bone-methods','Skin and musculoskeletal methods',['PHA-09','DER-01','DER-09','ORT-08','LON-03','DER-03','ORT-07','CRM-09','ORT-04'])
b.save()
